1. DEFINITIONS

1.1 "Software" means the MintStacks desktop application, including without limitation the executable files, the installer package, any source files, configuration files, documentation, updates, patches, and any components delivered therewith or made available to You by the Developer.

1.2 "Developer" means the individual creator of MintStacks, together with any contributors, licensors, and successors who publish or distribute the Software.

1.3 "User Data" means any file, folder, document, image, database, log, configuration, prompt, staged file list, backup, backup manifest, backup history entry, or any other electronic material that is accessed, read, copied, backed up, restored, edited, created, or deleted by the Software, including material that belongs to You, material that belongs to a third party, and material stored on or transmitted through any device under Your control.

1.4 "Telegram" means the messaging platform operated by Telegram FZ-LLC and its affiliates, used by the Software for the transmission of status notifications, nudge events, support chat messages, and related informational signals.

1.5 "Mintmark" means a user created shortcut to a folder on disk that the Software uses as the anchor for backups, staging, and related operations.

1.6 "Backup" means any full, changed, prompt, or other backup folder written by the Software.

1.7 "Restore" means any operation in which the Software copies files from a backup folder back into a target location.

1.8 "App ID" means the random identifier generated by the Software on first launch and persisted to the local user data folder, used to associate Your installation with support communications and nudge status.

1.9 "Nudge" means any notification presented by the Software asking You to support the project.

1.10 "DeNudge" means the mechanism by which the nudge system may be silenced on an installation following the Developer verification of a donation.


