8. DATA TRANSMISSION AND TELEGRAM INTEGRATION

8.1 The Software uses Telegram to transmit certain informational signals to the Developer. These transmissions are made for the purpose of tracking application usage, monitoring the health and adoption of the Software, and receiving support communications. The transmissions include, without limitation, the following events:

  (a) A "Ping" notification transmitted when the Software is launched, which includes the application version, the App ID, a country code derived from Your public IP address, and the current nudge status of Your installation.

  (b) A "Nudge" notification transmitted when a nudge event fires, which includes the App ID, the application version, and the trigger that fired.

  (c) A "Status" notification transmitted when a DeNudge key is applied to Your installation, which includes the application version and the App ID.

  (d) A "DeNudge Wrong Key" notification transmitted when a DeNudge key fails to verify, which includes the App ID, the application version, and the attempted key.

  (e) A "PayPal Request" notification transmitted when You request PayPal donation information through the Support page, which includes the App ID, a country code, the amount You entered, and any comment You provided.

  (f) A "Donation Curiosity" notification transmitted when a donation related page is opened or a donation badge is clicked, which includes the App ID, a country code, the current nudge status, the event details, and, for coin events, the coin name and coin address.

  (g) "MintTalk" support messages, which are private chat messages between You and the Developer, transmitted through the Telegram platform and stored locally on Your device.

  (h) "StacksTalk" and "MintNews" feed retrievals, which read public channel content from the Developer Telegram channel.

8.2 You acknowledge that these transmissions travel through the Telegram platform and are therefore subject to Telegram own privacy practices, terms of service, and technical infrastructure. You acknowledge that the Developer does not control Telegram and is not responsible for the security, availability, or privacy practices of the Telegram platform.

8.3 The Developer does not sell, rent, lease, license, trade, or otherwise disclose Your data to any third party.

8.4 The App ID stored on Your device is a random string generated on first launch and bound to a machine fingerprint. It is not derived from Your name, email address, or any other personal information.

8.5 The Software derives a country code from Your public IP address by querying a third party geolocation lookup service. The derived country code is cached locally on Your device for up to twenty four hours. The country code, and only the country code, is transmitted to the Developer as part of the Ping notification described in Section 8.1(a). The Software does not transmit Your IP address to the Developer.

8.6 You acknowledge that the transmissions described in this Section 8 are a condition of using the Software as distributed and that You have reviewed and accepted them by clicking the acceptance control presented by the installer.

8.7 The Software caches certain data locally on Your device, including feed content, message history, and geolocation country codes. This data remains on Your device except as described in this Section 8.


9. THIRD PARTY SERVICES

9.1 The Software interacts with third party services including, without limitation, the Telegram messaging platform, the Microsoft Windows operating system, and public IP geolocation lookup services. Your use of those services is governed by their own terms and privacy practices, and the Developer is not responsible for the availability, accuracy, security, or practices of those services.

9.2 The Software may contain links to third party websites or resources, including the community page reachable from the Mints button. The Developer provides those links for convenience only and does not endorse, control, or assume responsibility for the content, products, or services of any third party site.


10. BACKUP, RESTORE, AND FILE OPERATIONS

10.1 You acknowledge that the Software backup and restore functionality performs real file operations on real filesystems. A backup copies files from a source folder to one or more destination folders. A restore copies files from a backup folder back into a source folder, and may delete files that exist in the source but not in the backup manifest.

10.2 A restore is a destructive operation. Files that exist in the target location but are absent from the backup being restored will be deleted. You acknowledge this behavior and agree that You are solely responsible for verifying that the correct backup has been selected before authorizing a restore.

10.3 A backup may be incomplete for reasons outside the Developer control, including without limitation: files that are locked by other processes, files that are deleted or replaced during the backup walk, files that exceed filesystem limits, permission errors, disk space exhaustion, and network or removable drive disconnection.

10.4 You acknowledge that the Software restore resolver reconstructs the state of a target folder by reading the chain of backup manifests. If any backup in the chain is missing, deleted, moved, or corrupted, the resolver may be unable to reconstruct the target state and may report files as missing. You agree that You are solely responsible for maintaining the integrity of Your backup chain.

10.5 The Developer does not warrant that any backup will be restorable, that any restore will produce the exact state recorded, that any file will be preserved, or that any operation will complete without error. You agree that You will independently verify the results of any backup or restore operation that matters to You.


11. NUDGE SYSTEM

11.1 The Software includes a nudge system that periodically presents notifications asking You to support the project. The nudge system operates as part of the Software as distributed and is not a user selectable setting.

11.2 A DeNudge key, when issued by the Developer and successfully applied to Your installation, silences the nudge system. A DeNudge key is issued by the Developer after the Developer verifies a donation. DeNudge is not a subscription and is not a recurring payment obligation.

11.3 You acknowledge that the nudge system and the DeNudge system are part of the Software as distributed, that the terms and conditions under which a DeNudge key is issued are determined by the Developer, and that the Developer may modify nudge behavior, nudge frequency, nudge timing, or nudge triggers at any time and that any such change takes effect on the next launch of the Software.


